## Bootstrap Protocol

### Step 1: Understand User Intent

```
IF user provides task in natural language:
    - Ask clarifying questions if ambiguous
    - Identify: what, where, platform, constraints
    - Draft `.claude/artifacts/current_task/TASK.md` with structured requirements when needed
    - Confirm understanding before proceeding
```

### Step 2: Load Context

```
READ: .claude/artifacts/current_task/TASK.md      - Current task note (create if needed)
READ: .claude/knowledge/platform.md               - Workspace platform details
READ: .claude/rules/workflows.md                  - Project-specific workflow rules
IF maintainer work is on `.claude/`, docs, tasks, or artifacts:
    READ: .claude/knowledge/focus_boundaries.md   - TP-AgentKit vs external-tooling classifier
```

### Step 3: Load Skills & Knowledge

```
READ: .claude/skills/_registry.md   - Available tools (check status!)
READ: .claude/knowledge/*.md        - Verified knowledge
READ: .claude/rules/workflows.md    - Workflow policies
```

### Step 4: Discover Test Programs

```
testprogram/ may be gitignored or may not yet contain the requested revision folder.
DO NOT conclude missing from a single exact-path check.
USE: recursive discovery on key files (`*.ls`, `*.tpl`) + keyword matching, then fallback checks in `.claude/artifacts/current_task/` and `references/`.
FOLLOW: .claude/rules/workflows.md (Test Program Discovery)
```

### Step 5: Check Task State

```
IF .claude/artifacts/current_task/ EXISTS:
    READ: INDEX.md and the primary active artifact named there  - Resume from checkpoint
ELSE:
    CREATE: .claude/artifacts/current_task/
```

### Step 6: Prepare Safe Working Target

```
IF modifying anything under testprogram/<program>/:
    ASK: which revision to use, or whether a new revision copy should be created
    DEFAULT: copy the confirmed source folder to a new revision folder and edit only the copy
    KEEP: source folder unchanged for comparison
    ONLY IF user explicitly requests in-place work or backup-based handling:
        CREATE: testprogram/<program>_backup_<YYYYMMDD>/   (date only, no time)
        VERIFY: snapshot exists before proceeding
```

### Step 7: Confirmation Gate (MANDATORY)

BEFORE executing any file modifications:

1. Present plan summary to user
2. List all files that will be modified
3. Confirm source folder and working target folder
4. Confirm whether the workflow is revision copy or in-place backup
5. WAIT for explicit user approval
6. Accepted responses: "approved", "proceed", "go ahead", "yes"
7. DO NOT proceed without confirmation

